      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: We'll hear argument now in the case of Miller-El against Dretke."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Do we have to find that the strike of at least one African American prospective juror was race-based for you to prevail?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0000-0003",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the only evidence in the record that seems to me compels the conclusion that this was done for the deliberate purpose of minimizing the number of African Americans on the jury."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Waxman",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The jury shuffle is a practice that exists only in the State of Texas and, to my understanding, has ever existed only in the State of Texas."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Suppose that you have 10 white jurors and 10 black jurors. The 10 black jurors are all questioned much more extensively by the State, and in each of those cases, there is a plausible reason for excusing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BUNN: Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: The big picture. The majority of African Americans summoned for jury duty in this case were either opposed to the death penalty generally or unwilling to impose it, while the majority of white jurors had no qualms about the death penalty. Striking prospective jurors based on their case-related views which, after the fact, correlate with race is not unconstitutional."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: Well, I mean, I -- I am assuming it is relevant, and I am asking the question, is there a reasonable basis to think that these particular individuals, engaging in the practice that they demonstrably engaged in, had had a change in heart in this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The State requested shuffles three times."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Ms. Bunn, before you finish, there -- there are two pieces of this I hope you can give me an answer to. The race-coding. Is there any neutral reason for that? And when was that stopped, if it was?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Is it not a fair inference that each of the cues noted on the cards was something that the prosecutors thought relevant to whether or not to challenge the juror? And if so, is it not -- does -- is that not uncontradicted evidence that the race of the venire person was a factor in the decision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the State did question Mr. Fields on this issue during voir dire, and it was a basis for the strike."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-9659",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "7899400e6febf8d09cd30b43eb2c477ddcb30001bed175c3a4ae5e003921dc77",
      "evidence_id": "ev-7899400e6feb-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If you look at the Batson argument, it's either Mr. Macaluso or Mr. Nelson said some of the jurors were questioned disparately, but -- and they gave the explanation that it had to do with views on the death penalty."
    }
  ],
